\b Question 15\b0 : Dart and Flutter SDK Verification\par
1. Identify the commands used to check the installed Dart and Flutter versions.\par
- Dart version:\par
dart --version\par
- Flutter version:\par
flutter --version\par
2. Explain how the flutter doctor command helps identify problems in the development environment.\par
The flutter doctor command checks whether Flutter and the required development tools are correctly installed and configured.\par
It helps identify problems such as:\par
- Missing Android SDK.\par
- Incorrect Flutter configuration.\par
- Missing development tools.\par
- Unaccepted Android licenses.\par
- Problems with the development environment.\par
3. Describe the steps involved in accepting Android SDK licenses.\par
1. Open Command Prompt or Terminal.\par
2. Run the following command:\par
flutter doctor --android-licenses\par
3. Press Enter.\par
4. Type y whenever you are asked to accept a license.\par
5. Continue until all licenses are accepted.\par
Successful output:\par
All SDK package licenses accepted\par
4. Explain why it is important to verify development tools before starting application development.\par
- To ensure all required tools are installed.\par
- To identify and fix errors early.\par
- To ensure Flutter can detect the Android SDK.\par
- To avoid problems when building and running applications.\par
- To create a properly configured development environment.\par
