\b Question 17\b0 : Student Marks Management\par
Question: Write a Dart program that creates a List of five students' marks and performs different List operations.\par
Answer:\par
void main() \{\par
  // Creating a List of five students' marks\par
  List<int> marks = [70, 85, 60, 90, 75];\par
  // Displaying the second student's mark\par
  print("Second student's mark: $\{marks[1]\}");\par
  // Adding one mark\par
  marks.add(80);\par
  // Adding two marks\par
  marks.addAll([65, 95]);\par
  // Removing one mark using its index\par
  marks.removeAt(2);\par
  // Displaying all marks\par
  print("Student marks: $marks");\par
  // Displaying total number of marks\par
  print("Total marks: $\{marks.length\}");\par
  // Checking whether 80 exists\par
  print("Does 80 exist? $\{marks.contains(80)\}");\par
\}\par
Expected output:\par
Second student's mark: 85\par
Student marks: [70, 85, 90, 75, 80, 65, 95]\par
Total marks: 7\par
Does 80 exist? true\par
\par
Explanation of List methods:\par
Method\tab Purpose\par
List<int>\tab Creates a list of integers.\par
marks[1]\tab Accesses the second item.\par
add()\tab Adds one item.\par
addAll()\tab Adds multiple items.\par
removeAt(2)\tab Removes the item at index 2.\par
length\tab Counts the items in a list.\par
contains(80)\tab Checks whether 80 exists.\par
Important for exams\par
Dart List indexes start from zero:\par
Index:  0   1   2   3   4\par
Marks: 70  85  60  90  75\par
\par
Therefore, marks[1] displays 85, not 70.\par
