\b Question 18\b0 : Unique Student Registration\par
Question: Write a Dart program that uses a Set to store unique student registration numbers.\par
Answer:\par
void main() \{\par
  // Creating a Set of five registration numbers\par
  Set<int> registrationNumbers = \{101, 102, 103, 104, 105\};\par
  // Adding two new registration numbers\par
  registrationNumbers.add(106);\par
  registrationNumbers.add(107);\par
  // Attempting to add a duplicate\par
  registrationNumbers.add(103);\par
  // Checking whether a registration number exists\par
  print("Does 103 exist? $\{registrationNumbers.contains(103)\}");\par
  // Displaying unique registration numbers\par
  print("Registration numbers: $registrationNumbers");\par
  // Displaying total unique registration numbers\par
  print("Total unique students: $\{registrationNumbers.length\}");\par
  // Creating another Set\par
  Set<int> otherNumbers = \{104, 105, 108, 109\};\par
  // Union operation\par
  print("Union: $\{registrationNumbers.union(otherNumbers)\}");\par
  // Intersection operation\par
  print("Intersection: $\{registrationNumbers.intersection(otherNumbers)\}");\par
\}\par
\par
Expected output:\par
Does 103 exist? true\par
Registration numbers: \{101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107\}\par
Total unique students: 7\par
Union: \{101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107, 108, 109\}\par
Intersection: \{104, 105\}\par
Explanation of Set methods:\par
Method\tab Purpose\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 Set<int>\tab Creates a collection of unique integers.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}add()\tab Adds one unique item.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}contains()\tab Checks whether an item exists.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}length\tab Counts unique items.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}union()\tab Combines two Sets without duplicates.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}intersection()\tab Returns common items in two Sets.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Important: A Set does not allow duplicate values. When we add 103 again, Dart ignores the duplicate.\par

