\b Question 19\b0 : Student Information Management Using Map\par
Question: Write a Dart program that stores student information using key-value pairs.\par
Answer:\par
void main() \{\par
  // Creating a Map\par
  Map<String, dynamic> student = \{\par
    "name": "Chrisostome",\par
    "age": 12,\par
    "school": "CMS UNILAK",\par
    "status": true\par
  \};\par
  // Displaying student's name and age\par
  print("Student Name: $\{student["name"]\}");\par
  print("Student Age: $\{student["age"]\}");\par
  // Updating student's age\par
  student["age"] = 21;\par
  // Adding department\par
  student["department"] = "Software Development";\par
  // Checking whether department exists\par
  print("Department exists: $\{student.containsKey("department")\}");\par
  // Removing school information\par
  student.remove("school");\par
  // Displaying remaining keys and values\par
  print("Remaining student information:");\par
  print("Keys: $\{student.keys\}");\par
  print("Values: $\{student.values\}");\par
\}\par
Expected output:\par
Student Name: Chrisostome\par
Student Age: 12\par
\par
Department exists: true\par
\par
Remaining student information:\par
Keys: (name, age, status, department)\par
Values: (Chrisostome, 21, true, Software Development)\par
Explanation of Map methods:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1 Method\tab Purpose\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Map<String, dynamic>\tab Stores key-value pairs.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}student["name"]\tab Accesses the value using its key.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}student["age"] = 21\tab Updates an existing value.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}containsKey()\tab Checks whether a key exists.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}remove()\tab Removes a key-value pair.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}keys\tab Displays all keys.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}values\tab Displays all values.\par

