\b Question 21\b0 : Student Examination Results\par
Question: Write a Dart program that evaluates students' examination performance and assigns grades using if, else if and else.\par
\par
Grading system:\par
Marks\tab Grade\par
80\f2\endash\f1 100\tab Excellent\par
70\f2\endash\f1 79\tab Very Good\par
50\f2\endash\f1 69\tab Pass\par
Below 50\tab Fail\par
Answer:\par
void main() \{\par
  // Declaring student information\par
  String studentName = "Chrisostome";\par
  int marks = 85;\par
  String grade;\par
  // Checking student's performance\par
  if (marks >= 80 && marks <= 100) \{\par
    grade = "Excellent";\par
  \} else if (marks >= 70 && marks < 80) \{\par
    grade = "Very Good";\par
  \} else if (marks >= 50 && marks < 70) \{\par
    grade = "Pass";\par
  \} else \{\par
    grade = "Fail";\par
  \}\par
  // Displaying student information\par
  print("STUDENT EXAMINATION RESULTS");\par
  print("Student Name: $studentName");\par
  print("Marks: $marks");\par
  print("Grade: $grade");\par
\}\par
Expected output:\par
STUDENT EXAMINATION RESULTS\par
Student Name: Chrisostome\par
Marks: 85\par
Grade: Excellent\par
Explanation:\par
- if: Checks whether marks are between 80 and 100.\par
- else if: Checks another condition when the previous condition is false.\par
- else: Executes when none of the previous conditions is true.\par
- &&: Means AND. Both conditions must be true.\par
- grade: Stores the result of the student's performance.\par
Sequential execution:\par
Sequential execution means instructions run one after another, from top to bottom.\par
In this program:\par
1. The student's name is declared.\par
2. The examination marks are declared.\par
3. The program checks the marks.\par
4. The grade is assigned.\par
5. The student's information is displayed.\par
}
